  "query_preview": "below remain valid. \n\nOne big question for Tuesday is how much convection we see overnight \ninto Tuesday morning. 17.00z hi-res guidance seems to be keying off \nof another wave and the LLJ moving through the area behind the \nsurface front through the overnight hours into the Tuesday morning \ncommute, more so than previous runs. Instability should wane quickly \nthrough the overnight, so severe weather threat is low after \nmidnight/1 AM CDT. However, morning storms and convective debris \nwill impact severe potential later in the day with the greatest \nrisks toward the MO River Valley and US Hwy 20, although some \nguidance is a bit further north.",
